e rotation, not an abrupt regime switch."}, "raw_final_response": "**Analysis summary:**\n\n- **step_01** (prescribed method, half-window 5000): peak dissimilarity = **0.2683** at t=81322 \u2014 far below the 0.6 threshold. Before/after contact sets share ~33 of ~37 contacts.\n- **step_10** (half-window 3000, robustness): peak = 0.3333, still well below threshold; series is flat/low throughout (0.03\u20130.33), i.e. gradual background churn, no localized spike.\n- **step_02 / step_06**: group activity is roughly constant (~74 events/bin, no bursts), so no volume artifact could hide or manufacture a transition.\n- **step_05**: edge-level Jaccard is 0.0 between the first and last 5000-unit windows, but the *added* and *removed* edges point to the **same contact pool** (58, 138, 247, 383, 393, 402, ... 1999) \u2014 only the group member acting as source rotates (59/83 early, 991/1034 late; confirmed by **step_09** and **step_08**). This is intra-group role rotation over a fixed neighbourhood, not a replacement of the group's partners.\n- **step_07**: members are only weakly co-active, consistent with staggered individual activity rather than a synchronized group-wide switch.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8155967f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [59, 83, 325, 610, 617, 642, 743, 826, 881, 991, 1034, 1641],\n  \"window\": [56322, 86322],\n  \"confidence\": 0.86,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"With the prescribed 5000-unit half-window, peak before/after contact-set dissimilarity is 0.2683 (at t=81322), well under the 0.6 criterion, and the turnover series is uniformly low (0.12-0.27) with no localized jump; a 3000-unit half-window gives at most 0.33. Edge-level snapshots do differ completely (Jaccard 0.0), but the added and removed edges terminate on the same partner pool - only which group member is the active source rotates over time (59/83 early, 991/1034 late). Group event volume is flat with no bursts, ruling out volume-driven artifacts. Conclusion: gradual background turnover plus intra-group role rotation, not an abrupt regime switch.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 44237, "total_output_tokens": 3595, "total_tokens": 47832, "total_latency_ms": 54828, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}